Table core.OperatingDayException {
  Note: '''
Override an individual calendar date as a holiday or extra working day.

The dispatcher checks this table before firing time-based notifications.
When `is_holiday=True`, the date is skipped even if the operating_days_bitmask
would normally allow it. (Future: is_holiday=False would mark a normally-off day
as working, but the dispatcher doesn't use that path yet.)

DDL: core.operating_day_exceptions
UNIQUE: date


*table: public.core_operating_day_exceptions*'''

  id big_auto [note: '''*ID*''', pk, unique, not null]
  date date [note: '''*date*''', unique, not null]
  is_holiday boolean [note: '''
*is holiday*
True = treat this date as non-operating (skip notifications).''', default:`True`, not null]
  note char [note: '''*note*''', default:`""`, not null]
  created_by_id big_auto [null]
  created_at date_time [note: '''*created at*''', not null]

  indexes {
