Table export.CustomsExpense {
  Note: '''
A single line of the customs/document cash-advance ledger (money-OUT side).

Context: the cashier (e.g. Hangeldi) receives periodic float top-ups
(FinansistAdvance, the money-IN side) and spends cash on per-truck or
batch customs/document fees.  This model records each expenditure.

Per-shipment fees (gumrukleme, fito, analiz, …) link to a Shipment via FK.
Batch fees covering a group of shipments (e.g. "19 AD KARANTIN") set
shipment=NULL and use the ``quantity`` field to store the unit count.

Currency is TMT (Turkmen manat) by default — unlike FinansistAdvance which
uses USD for advance float-ups.  A non-TMT row is valid but rare.

The ledger balance at any point = sum(FinansistAdvance.total_amount) in TMT
minus sum(CustomsExpense.amount).  See views_finance.py CustomsExpenseViewSet
for the /ledger/ summary action.


*table: public.export_customs_expenses*'''

  id big_auto [note: '''*ID*''', pk, unique, not null]
  expense_date date [note: '''*expense date*''', not null]
  category export.char_customsexpense_category [note: '''*category*''', not null]
  amount decimal [note: '''*amount*''', not null]
  currency char [note: '''*currency*''', default:`"TMT"`, not null]
  shipment_id big_auto [null]
  export_code_raw char [note: '''*export code raw*''', null]
  vehicle_plate char [note: '''*vehicle plate*''', null]
  route_label char [note: '''*route label*''', null]
  label_raw char [note: '''*label raw*''', null]
  quantity positive_small_integer [note: '''
*quantity*
Unit count for batch fees, e.g. 19 for \"19 AD KARANTIN\".''', null]
  notes char [note: '''*notes*''', null]
  created_by_id big_auto [not null]
  created_at date_time [note: '''*created at*''', not null]

  indexes {
    (category) [name: 'customs_exp_category_idx', type: btree]
    (expense_date) [name: 'customs_exp_date_idx', type: btree]
    (shipment_id) [name: 'customs_exp_shipment_idx', type: btree]
    (created_by_id) [name: 'export_customs_expenses_created_by_id_c6e83e71', type: btree]
    (id) [pk, unique, name: 'export_customs_expenses_pkey', type: btree]
    (shipment_id) [name: 'export_customs_expenses_shipment_id_3f8ec429', type: btree]
  }
}
ref: export.CustomsExpense.shipment_id > export.Shipment.id
ref: export.CustomsExpense.created_by_id > core.User.id


