Table feedback.FeedbackReply {
  Note: '''
Admin reply to a feedback ticket.

Supports three modes:
- standard: visible to both the author and admin (default response)
- internal: admin-only note, hidden from the ticket author
- public: promoted to the Public Feed along with the parent ticket

is_internal and is_public are denormalised booleans synced from mode on save().
This ensures the DB cannot enter an inconsistent state.


*table: public.feedback_feedbackreply*'''

  id big_auto [note: '''*ID*''', pk, unique, not null]
  ticket_id big_auto [not null]
  author_id big_auto [not null]
  content char [note: '''*content*''', not null]
  mode feedback.char_feedbackreply_mode [note: '''*mode*''', default:`"standard"`, not null]
  is_internal boolean [note: '''*is internal*''', default:`False`, not null]
  is_public boolean [note: '''*is public*''', default:`False`, not null]
  created_at date_time [note: '''*created at*''', not null]

  indexes {
    (author_id) [name: 'feedback_feedbackreply_author_id_f04096ea', type: btree]
    (id) [pk, unique, name: 'feedback_feedbackreply_pkey', type: btree]
    (ticket_id) [name: 'feedback_feedbackreply_ticket_id_fcdc5c3a', type: btree]
  }
}
